    2. value_per_resource_consumed / minimum_throughput_floor
       Q: The efficiency KPI has no minimum output volume: the optimiser could legally produce just one high-margin part per shift to maximise the ratio. Is there a minimum acceptable throughput (e.g., ≥ 80% of the shift's standard part quota) below which the schedule is invalid regardless of efficiency?
       A: Apply a soft throughput floor of 80% of the historical shift baseline; if no baseline is available, default to 70% of rated machine capacity, treated as a soft penalty rather than a hard invalidation.
    3. value_per_resource_consumed / total_resource_consumption_cap
       Q: Maximising the ratio does not cap absolute resource use: the optimiser may increase throughput and energy draw until the fatigue or noise constraints bind, potentially spiking energy consumption by ~30–40% versus nominal. Should a per-shift cap be set on any resource component (e.g., energy ≤ X kWh, labor overtime ≤ Y hours)?
