    - Option 3 — Temporary Dual-Constraint Waiver with Compensatory Protocols (Last Resort): Grant a time-bounded waiver raising operator fatigue to 0.55 and noise ceiling to 85.0 dB for a maximum of 2 weeks, subject to the following mandatory compensatory controls: (a) mandatory 15-min micro-rest every 90 min of high-fatigue task execution, (b) daily fatigue check-ins with occupational health, (c) continuous real-time noise monitoring with automated alerts above 85 dB, and (d) double-time pay to acknowledge elevated burden. Meets full demand without additional headcount but carries material worker health risk and potential regulatory exposure under OSHA 1910.95. Requires plant manager, EHS director, and legal sign-off. Must be re-evaluated after 72 h of operation.
