       Q: Operator labor-hours appear in the efficiency denominator, so the optimiser gains ratio points by reducing headcount or shortening active work time — but fewer operators doing the same work drives individual fatigue toward the 0.4 ceiling; should labor-hours be excluded from the efficiency denominator, or should fatigue be modelled per-operator rather than as a crew aggregate?
