    2. resource_efficiency (no per-resource-type ceiling)
       Q: Maximising resource_efficiency with no cap on individual resource categories means the optimiser could legally cut labour hours by running machinery ~40% harder and faster — should any single resource type carry a ceiling (e.g. energy ≤ X kWh per shift, or machine utilisation ≤ Y%) to prevent unsafe substitution between resource types?
