    - Option 2 — Engineering Noise Controls + Noise Limit Temporary Uplift: Deploy immediate acoustic engineering controls (close-fitting machine enclosures, anti-vibration mounts, mandatory fitted ear protection rated to at least NRR-15) to reduce effective operator noise dose. Request a temporary, time-bounded uplift of the noise ceiling from 80.0 dB to 83.0 dB for a maximum of 14 calendar days while permanent controls are installed. This addresses the noise violation but does not resolve operator fatigue; a secondary measure (e.g., enforced 20-minute rest breaks every 90 minutes) must accompany this option to partially reduce fatigue toward the 0.40 threshold. Expected residual fatigue gap after rest-break insertion: approximately 8–10% of demand must be deferred.
