    - Option 3 — Accept Partial Demand Deferral with No Constraint Relaxation: Freeze the schedule at maximum throughput achievable within both existing hard limits (fatigue <= 0.40, noise <= 80.0 dB). The resulting production output covers approximately 83% of the increased demand target. The remaining ~17% of orders are formally deferred to the next planning horizon or re-routed to an alternate facility if available. No operator health constraint is relaxed. The production manager must notify customer-facing teams and initiate customer communication for affected orders. This option preserves full regulatory and ethical compliance at the cost of a known, quantified service shortfall.
