    - Option 3 — Formal Dual-Constraint Waiver with Enhanced Monitoring: Request a time-bounded formal waiver for both constraints: operator fatigue ceiling raised from 0.40 to 0.47 (capped at the current violation level, no further increase permitted), and noise ceiling raised from 80.0 dB to 85.0 dB. Mandatory mitigations must accompany approval: (a) real-time biometric fatigue monitoring with automatic workstation alerts at 0.45, (b) enhanced PPE for all personnel in high-noise zones, (c) daily occupational-health check-ins, and (d) automatic waiver expiry after 10 working days or when demand normalises, whichever comes first. This option fully closes the demand-deadline gap with zero schedule disruption but is the least desirable from a worker-welfare standpoint and requires sign-off from both the production manager and the site safety officer before the CBPA scheduler will accept it.
